The proof does the same coordinate argument three times, with only the constants (−785, −11872, −2875) and the index (0, 1, 2) changing. The repeated parts are:
(1) the formula c0/c1/c2, `rem astar d p i = ((a_i*d − 50000*p i : ℤ):ℝ)/50000`;
(2) the upper bound b0/b1/b2, which rewrites the residue to r_i via `hz` and uses `normcoord` and `hM_i`;
(3) the three-way `rcases hMa` branches, which apply `abs_residue_le 50000 r_i (a_i*d) …` after `norm_le_pi_norm … i`.
Each copy has the same shape but is edited by hand per coordinate, which invites copy errors.
